WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.157 --> 00:00:03.374
- By a show of hands, how
many people are voting?

00:00:03.374 --> 00:00:07.425
How many people are excited
to vote for Hillary?

00:00:07.425 --> 00:00:10.798
My name's Darren Sands, I'm
a reporter with BuzzFeed News

00:00:10.798 --> 00:00:13.749
based in Washington DC,
and I cover politics.

00:00:13.749 --> 00:00:15.971
We're here in Tallahassee, Florida

00:00:15.971 --> 00:00:18.015
visiting Florida A&amp;M University,

00:00:18.015 --> 00:00:20.377
it's a historically black college.

00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:22.992
I'm trying to see where they are

00:00:22.992 --> 00:00:24.988
in terms of their decision-making.

00:00:24.988 --> 00:00:28.451
Whether they're gonna vote
and try to get a good sense

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:32.618
of what turnout is gonna
be like come November 8th.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.554
Meet up with right now is one of

00:00:36.554 --> 00:00:38.405
Clinton's organizers on campus

00:00:38.405 --> 00:00:41.420
and we got to see her interact
with this young student,

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.721
a freshman, and she was not
actually committed to vote

00:00:44.721 --> 00:00:45.745
- I don't know who to vote for.

00:00:45.745 --> 00:00:48.068
I'm not voting for Trump if
that's what you're asking.

00:00:48.068 --> 00:00:49.967
- You can be a leader, and say hey,

00:00:49.967 --> 00:00:51.916
I have a car, I'm a freshman as well,

00:00:51.916 --> 00:00:54.733
pack five, ten people in
your car, y'all sit on laps.

00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:56.804
- Yeah.
- It's a short drive.

00:00:56.804 --> 00:01:00.253
- They see you, you know, the
more they're likely to vote,

00:01:00.253 --> 00:01:01.842
cause now that's a reminder, like oh,

00:01:01.842 --> 00:01:03.311
that's the voter registration lady.

00:01:03.311 --> 00:01:05.991
You do care, you know
this is my university too,

00:01:05.991 --> 00:01:08.779
and I care about the students as well.

00:01:08.779 --> 00:01:10.392
- [Darren] We get a chance to meet

00:01:10.392 --> 00:01:13.145
the up and coming Mayor of Tallahassee,

00:01:13.145 --> 00:01:16.061
a young black Mayor by
the name of Andrew Gillum.

00:01:16.061 --> 00:01:18.457
- And I'll tell you, at least
on the social media side,

00:01:18.457 --> 00:01:21.589
you almost don't have to
do a pro-Hillary message

00:01:21.589 --> 00:01:23.683
because there's so much anti-Trump.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:27.239
- You think that affects
the enthusiasm that she has?

00:01:27.239 --> 00:01:30.642
- I'm over the enthusiasm question.

00:01:30.642 --> 00:01:31.946
- A lot of people are over it.

00:01:31.946 --> 00:01:35.041
- I'm over it and where I am is that

00:01:35.041 --> 00:01:37.146
this is a matter of our futures

00:01:37.146 --> 00:01:38.837
and our children's futures.

00:01:38.837 --> 00:01:43.111
As I have closed out many
of remarks to campuses

00:01:43.111 --> 00:01:45.739
and to students with,
elections are choices.

00:01:45.739 --> 00:01:48.656
That there's some perfect out there

00:01:50.495 --> 00:01:52.087
is not the case.

00:01:52.087 --> 00:01:54.164
I don't believe Obama was perfect,

00:01:54.164 --> 00:01:56.386
but I do believe that his intentions

00:01:56.386 --> 00:01:59.119
are consistent with my belief system.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.615
- And we talked to a lot of older voters,

00:02:01.615 --> 00:02:03.868
black voters, people who went to FAM,

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.624
and they recognize the students

00:02:05.624 --> 00:02:07.920
aren't that excited about Hillary.

00:02:07.920 --> 00:02:10.818
- Be honest with you, they are
not really feeling Hillary,

00:02:10.818 --> 00:02:12.414
I mean that's the truth to it.

00:02:12.414 --> 00:02:14.120
- I talked to a lot of the students

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:17.749
who weren't that excited
about Hillary Clinton

00:02:17.749 --> 00:02:20.549
- I've been hearing that a
lot from the young people.

00:02:20.549 --> 00:02:23.856
- Even though they don't
per se like Hillary

00:02:23.856 --> 00:02:25.591
they're gonna vote for her.

00:02:25.591 --> 00:02:27.258
- Trump scares me.

00:02:27.258 --> 00:02:28.946
I just really wish the candidates

00:02:28.946 --> 00:02:31.314
would have been stronger on both sides.

00:02:31.314 --> 00:02:36.310
- Also at the tailgate we got
the most enormous turkey leg

00:02:36.310 --> 00:02:39.643
that I have ever seen in my entire life.

00:02:41.416 --> 00:02:43.345
We go to the President's barbecue

00:02:43.345 --> 00:02:46.370
and we talk to about maybe ten students

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:49.357
who are at this table getting
ready to work the barbecue.

00:02:49.357 --> 00:02:51.832
How would you describe the
mood of the student body

00:02:51.832 --> 00:02:55.801
as it relates to the election
and to the candidates?

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.725
- I don't feel like anything
that we do at this point,

00:02:57.725 --> 00:02:59.311
or any person you can vote for

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:00.521
is going to be transparent about

00:03:00.521 --> 00:03:02.980
what exactly they're gonna
do while they're in office.

00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:05.861
And I don't have faith
that whatever anybody says

00:03:05.861 --> 00:03:07.840
that they're going to
do that they will do.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:10.126
Honestly, I had faith in a candidate,

00:03:10.126 --> 00:03:12.673
Bernie Sanders, but that
candidate's no longer there.

00:03:12.673 --> 00:03:16.180
- You go to Howard, Morgan
State, anywhere you went

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:19.379
they were basically all about Bernie,

00:03:19.379 --> 00:03:23.051
and that frustrated a lot of Democrats

00:03:23.051 --> 00:03:27.585
because you know, Bernie
wasn't a Democrat. (laughing)

00:03:27.585 --> 00:03:29.375
- We fought for this African
American thoughtfulness

00:03:29.375 --> 00:03:33.334
for decades, so the least
we could do is vote.

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:35.017
It's about, you know who we're voting for

00:03:35.017 --> 00:03:36.908
is gonna be the biggest thing,

00:03:36.908 --> 00:03:38.642
but just holding them accountable I think

00:03:38.642 --> 00:03:40.957
is gonna really make the most difference.

00:03:40.957 --> 00:03:43.945
- I feel like we can't risk Trump winning,

00:03:43.945 --> 00:03:45.680
so that's why I'm going to vote.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:48.236
- If I don't vote, that's
me endorsing both candidates

00:03:48.236 --> 00:03:50.235
everything, like in it's entirety.

00:03:50.235 --> 00:03:51.533
I feel like my vote matters

00:03:51.533 --> 00:03:53.410
because in all actuality it does.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:54.243
- By a show of hands,

00:03:54.243 --> 00:03:55.426
how many people have been canvassed

00:03:55.426 --> 00:03:56.703
and been asked if you're voting

00:03:56.703 --> 00:03:58.556
or if you've been registered to vote?

00:03:58.556 --> 00:03:59.846
So they've been canvassing

00:03:59.846 --> 00:04:01.994
pretty well on campus.
- Tirelessly.

00:04:01.994 --> 00:04:03.911
- Democrats are kind of

00:04:05.493 --> 00:04:08.939
very anxious that there's
gonna be a repeat of 2000.

00:04:08.939 --> 00:04:11.130
I think the campaign and also the DNC

00:04:11.130 --> 00:04:12.551
have taken that to heart.

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.313
They know that if they turn out the voters

00:04:15.313 --> 00:04:17.226
that they need to do,
they can win the election.

00:04:17.226 --> 00:04:20.774
So that's what makes
it a turnout election.

00:04:20.774 --> 00:04:24.382
Overall, we learned that
on this particular campus,

00:04:24.382 --> 00:04:26.619
no, voters are not that excited

00:04:26.619 --> 00:04:29.045
about casting a ballot
for Hillary Clinton.

00:04:29.045 --> 00:04:32.154
But they've all been
engaged by the campaign.

00:04:32.154 --> 00:04:33.750
They pretty much all have been asked

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:35.581
if they're registered to vote.

00:04:35.581 --> 00:04:38.044
They're registered to
vote and they're voting.

00:04:38.044 --> 00:04:40.483
Not only do they want to
make their voices heard,

00:04:40.483 --> 00:04:42.730
but they also want to make sure

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.651
that she can be held accountable

00:04:44.651 --> 00:04:47.836
for changes that can be
made with racial injustice,

00:04:47.836 --> 00:04:50.094
and that they don't
wanna actually disrespect

00:04:50.094 --> 00:04:53.839
the idea that people fought
for the right to vote,

00:04:53.839 --> 00:04:55.137
they died for the right to vote,

00:04:55.137 --> 00:04:57.987
they protested, blood was shed,

00:04:57.987 --> 00:05:02.154
and at FAM, that's something
that people don't take lightly.

